[Music]  [Applause]  hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to the  edition of ask Evan did I mention a  question from one of my face book  readers godson who wrote insane I want  to go into the magazine publication  business and I don't have any capital of  my own to start off but I need your  advice and how to go into magazine  publication so thanks for the question  and it's great to see you on facebook i  love my facebook readers  two quick tips for you first i would  look at going to find a job working for  somebody who's in that business if you  haven't had any experience in the  magazine business before go try to work  with somebody else who's already doing  what you want to do it'll do a couple  things for you first it'll teach you  about the industry so you'll make some  contacts you'll learn how to ropes what  the ropes are you'll learn how to do the  business you'll be able to see you know  how to basically run the day-to-day  operations so that when you do go out  and start your own business you know  what to do and what not to do so you're  basically getting paid to make all the  mistakes and learn on somebody else's  watch the second thing that will teach  you is do you want to do this business  or not so sometimes we get excited about  companies instead of a business ideas  but then once we get into it we realize  hey there's a lot of work or this isn't  what I thought it was gonna be you know  it's a great dream but I really feel  like I should be doing something else  and that's okay it's good that start  small test see if it's for you or not so  by going to work for somebody else you  get those contacts you get the the  experience and the connections but it  also teaches you if you should be doing  this business or not and again you're  doing it all on somebody else's dime and  so you're not spending your own money  yet to do it it'll be my first tip the  second thing is I always love as much as  possible to try to create a business  without spending any money so I'll  invest my time energy effort blood sweat  tears but not my money into starting  something new and so I try to encourage  entrepreneurs who's the same thing so  your long term goal may be to create a  magazine publication as your business  that's awesome how can you start that  off on a smaller scale where you're not  spending any money and one place you  might look to is the web so create a web  version of whatever magazine you're  trying to do if it's a lifestyle or  sports or whatever it is create a  website you're gonna need a website  anyway for your magazine and a lot of  magazines are even going to the web and  shutting down their magazines because  it's hard to keep up with the economic  model of having a print magazine but  start online and you'll start making  connection  and start getting some good story ideas  out there and it doesn't cost you a lot  of money to create a website or  hopefully any money compared to actually  creating the physical magazine and that  will help you start to grow the business  and if you can start charging some  advertising rates on there and make some  money and then pour that that profit  back into your business you will to  expand into hopefully your magazine  publication so just those two quick  things those are my quick tips for you  got Santa to get you past the hump one  can work for somebody else has already  done what you're trying to do to learn  from them and see if this is the type of  business that you want to do and to  figure out a way to start small without  spending any money I would personally  look at doing it online to start you may  find other ways through partnerships or  through working with another company at  the same time to launch a magazine but  again without spending any money try to  figure that out bootstrap it up and then  you can be able to expand from there one  last one last thought a lot of  entrepreneurs do try to go out and raise  capital for their business and it's  great it's a it's a great potential idea  that the two things to keep in mind  first of all it takes up a lot of time  so raising capital so I should be going  for angel Capital or venture capital it  almost becomes a full-time job and that  takes away from you being able to  actually run your business so I'd rather  invest that time into making my business  run and and launch instead of just  having the idea on paper that I'm  pitching around to investors the second  thing is if you were at the really early  stage you're gonna get killed on your  valuation if you go to a bank you're  gonna have to pay really high interest  rates if you go to any kind of other  investor equity investor they're gonna  take a big chunk of your company just  because you have an idea and you haven't  actually launched your business so the  more you can get momentum building some  real customers coming in even if you're  not making a lot of money but you're  making some money then if you need to  make money to go to expand and get get  some angel or venture capital investors  involved you'll get a much better  valuation because you have a lot more of  a track record behind you so hopefully  that helps godson for those of you  watching if you like the video please  give it a thumbs up makes fun of do more  videos for you and I'd love to hear what  you have to think you can leave a  comment under the video or if you have a  question for your own business I always  love hearing those so thank you and I'll  see you on the next episode  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]

